The retained `com.xenova.LogMelSpectrogram` kernel computes
`log(max(acc, params.logFloor)) * 0.43429448190325176`, then with
`clamp_to_peak=false` applies `(value + postAdd) * postScale`. The LFM3 audio
frontend passes `post_add: 4` and `post_scale: 1 / Wx`; the pinned `Wx` is 4.
Thus the required post-scale is 0.25, not 0.125.

`test/zoo/lfm3/audio/frontend.test.ts` independently compares the implementation
FFT with a direct DFT and Slaney filter calculation using this normalization.
The full ruNNtime unit suite passed (55 files, 1,165 tests). This is frontend
operator evidence only: no clean audio clip or same-file Liquid encoder output
was available, and it does not qualify transcription or speech generation.
